.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_DELAY 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_delay ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_delay_total ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_delay_batch
.Nd advance the timestamps of records
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_delay "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_delay_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_delay_total "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_delay_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_delay_batch "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_delay_batch_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_stream_delay
re-times each record of
.Fa st
to the time
.Fn fn
returns for it, which must be greater than or equal to the record's
current time, and releases the record at the new time once the input
frontier has passed it.
The callback
.Fa fn
receives the record bytes, its length, the current time, and a buffer
.Fa new_time
of the scope's class to fill.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_delay_total
is
.Fn dtfl_stream_delay
specialised to a totally ordered time; its behaviour is identical.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_delay_batch
re-times whole messages: the callback sees only the message time, not
the records, and all records of a message move together to the new
time.
.Pp
A re-timed time that is not greater than or equal to the old time is a
contract violation and panics through the panic hook.
The context
.Fa ctx
is released by its destructor when the operator is dropped (PLAN D5).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Each function returns the re-timed stream, carrying the same record
type as
.Fa st .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/* Move each record i (all fed at time 0) to time i. */
static void to_value(void *c, const void *rec, size_t len,
    const uint64_t *t, uint64_t *nt) { *nt = dtfl_get_u64(rec); }
dtfl_stream *out = dtfl_stream_delay(s, to_value, DTFL_NOCTX);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_stream_reclock 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_unary_notify 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Vt Delay
trait.
It is public at the pinned release
.Pq Li timely-v0.31.0
and was removed upstream afterward (#818); the port keeps the pinned
behavior.
The
.Fn unary_frontier
equivalent buffers records per time and releases them when a
notificator reports the time complete.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The streams and the operator belong to the thread that runs the worker
and must not be used from another thread (PLAN section 5).
